<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22145" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnaequālĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		2. in-aequalis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unevenness</i>, <i>unlikeness</i>,
				<i>inequality</i> (not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">togae et tunicae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 8, § 28</span></i>
			 Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inaequalitate dissident (supercilia),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coloris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 9, 17</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 3,
			43</span></i>.—In plur., <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 12,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 70, 70, §
			177</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>grammatical irregularity</i>, <i>anomaly</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 9, § 3</span></i>
			Müll.; <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 25, 3</span></i>.</div>
